WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:02.900
- Hi everyone, my name is Luka Negoita

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.570
and I'm an ecologist and a data scientist

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.781
and I've always wanted
to make a course on R

00:00:07.781 --> 00:00:12.418
that I wish I had as a grad
student going into ecology.

00:00:12.418 --> 00:00:14.690
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.320
I think that one of the hardest parts

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.380
with starting a grad program in ecology

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.830
is really getting a good grasp of R.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.630
And it's frustrating because R is a tool

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.370
that should help us do good science,

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.150
not stand in the way of it.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:28.340
The point of this course
is really to eliminate

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.190
that frustration and anxiety

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.300
so that you can really start plotting

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.290
and exploring your data on your own

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.050
and feel really comfortable doing it.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.260
The project-based lessons and exercises

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.530
in this course are designed
to take you by the hand

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:43.000
through the most essential tools in R,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.530
beginning with things as simple

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:46.480
as how to install R and RStudio,

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.020
how to upload your own data

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.490
but then getting into the
more advanced data wrangling,

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:53.810
data management, creating
publication-quality figures,

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.890
learning how to organize your projects

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.340
and doing all of this while
feeling really confident.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.160
Now, this course doesn't
cover any data analysis

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.540
or modeling but that's really the point.

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.220
There's a lot of R courses out there

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.840
that try to cover everything

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.420
and I think that can be really
overwhelming for beginners

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.180
to really grasp the foundation.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.020
This course is designed
for students in ecology,

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.280
whether you're a grad student

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.620
or an undergraduate student.

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.380
But really this course
is applicable to anyone

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.960
that wants a solid foundation
in the basics of R.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.080
If you're interested in this course,

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.870
check out the link
below in the description

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:24.972
so you can register.

00:01:24.972 --> 00:01:26.980
Registration for this initial launch

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.660
I only open for one week.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.360
So make sure you register
as soon as you can.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.650
Thank you so much for watching

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.400
and please share this with anyone

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.716
that you could benefit from this course.

00:01:36.716 --> 00:01:39.299
(lively music)

